From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.12 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: ipq95xx: declare Spectrum SBE1V1K LAN/WAN ports

Without a spectrum,sbe1v1k case, board.d/02_network falls through to
"Unsupported hardware" and package/base-files' 99-default_network
writes lan=eth0 / wan=eth1.  That is both incomplete (two of the four
ports) and wrong: on this board eth0 is the RTL8261N 10G WAN and
eth1/eth2/eth3 are the QCA8081/QCA8075 LAN ports (see patches/0011).

LuCI builds the status -> overview port panel from the board.json
network section (luci-mod-status 29_ports.js): it reads lan.ports[]
and wan.device, so the fallback leaves two ports showing with the
roles reversed.  ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan() emits a
space-separated LAN list as a "ports" array, which is exactly the
shape 29_ports.js expects.

Status: static only, NOT TESTED on hardware.
---
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@
 	qcom,ipq9574-ap-al02-c7)
 		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "lan1 lan2 lan3 lan4 lan5" "wan"
 		;;
+	spectrum,sbe1v1k)
+		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "eth1 eth2 eth3" "eth0"
+		;;
 	*)
 		echo "Unsupported hardware. Network interfaces not initialized"
 		;;
